WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.710
Vostok station, Antarctica, 21 July 1983:

2
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.810
minus 89.2 degrees Celsius.

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.530
The lowest temperature ever
recorded on Earth's surface.

4
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:18.270
The coldest, windiest, driest continent,
with gusts of well over 200 kilometres

5
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.530
an hour.

6
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.090
In winter there is little
or no sunlight at all.

7
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.630
Yet emperor penguins live here.

8
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:31.170
On the treeless Arctic tundra, even July
averages no more than 10 degrees Celsius.

9
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.630
So how does anything live there?

10
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.530
Does it all sleep through winter?

11
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.670
Does very little live there at all?

12
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.490
In this mission, you'll find out
why Antarctica is so cold and dry.

13
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.090
Then you'll find out how plants
and animals survive there.

14
00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.760
Your mission: explain how life
survives in Earth's coldest places.
